CAGRA PQ-ADC for GINflow
=======================

This directory contains a CAGRA-style GPU graph index whose search kernel
evaluates node-level product-quantized sliding windows with Asymmetric
Distance Computation (ADC) from a shared-memory lookup table.

Portions of the graph traversal, visited hashmap, and reverse-edge / prune
construction are adapted from NVIDIA cuVS CAGRA:

  https://github.com/rapidsai/cuvs
  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2023-2026, NVIDIA CORPORATION & AFFILIATES.
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

cuVS CAGRA does not expose a custom device distance.  The dataset descriptor
and `compute_distance` path in cuVS are closed over float/half/int8 and VPQ
layouts that operate on a single concatenated vector.  GINflow instead stores
one PQ code per node, forms windows of those codes, and needs

    score(q, db) = sum_p sum_m LUT[p][m][db_code[p][m]]

with the LUT built from the original (unquantized) query node subvectors.
That is the modification applied here.

Node-level PQ training, window slicing, and the Python API are original
GINflow code.
